            <div xml:id="d369">

                <pb facs="0485" n="391" xml:id="pg391"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.5048/375: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Geneva</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gilbert</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-12-26T11:00:00+01:00">December 26, 1930—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 26—7:37 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Consulate’s December 18, 9 a.m.<anchor n="55" xml:id="d369-f1"/> Am informed that
                    League has received formal note from British Government requesting that Liberian
                    inquiry report be placed on the agenda of the next meeting of the Council. In
                    order to be placed on the agenda, action is required by the Council at its first
                    meeting. This action, however, is regarded as merely <hi rendition="#italic">pro
                        forma.</hi></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gilbert</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
